'' 'redim a( 2 to 6, 3 to 12 ) as T' IN A TYPE is a dynamic array FIELD sized by the constructor;
'' '( any )' leaves it unsized and '( 4 )' starts at 0 (fbc's fbc-int/array.bas). tiko made it a
'' variable of the type's scope with no storage, and indexing it faulted. Expected output is fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/redim-field.bas -o tests/codegen/redimfield.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/redimfield.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2 6 3 12 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  5z
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  12
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  3            -1             0             4
